This tree follows the [Irminsul](https://github.com/huajie-zhong/Irminsul) layout.

## Navigation Protocol

The documentation is organized by layer, and each layer sets the rules its docs follow.

| Layer | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| [foundation/](foundation/INDEX.md) | Why the system exists; core principles. |
| [architecture/](architecture/INDEX.md) | How the parts fit and how data flows between them. |
| [components/](components/INDEX.md) | One doc per architectural piece; maps code to concepts. |
| [decisions/](decisions/INDEX.md) | ADRs; the record of trade-offs. |
| [rfcs/](rfcs/INDEX.md) | Proposals moving through the change lifecycle. |
| [guides/](guides/INDEX.md) | How-tos, operations, and docs about this doc system. |

## For AI Agents and Contributors

- **Code Mapping:** Every component doc in `components/` contains a `describes:` frontmatter field mapping it to source files.
- **Stability:** Refer to the `status:` field (draft | stable | deprecated | removed) to understand the reliability of a document.
- **Discovery:** Start with `irminsul orient`, run `irminsul context <path>` before editing a known source or doc path, and use `irminsul context --changed` after editing.

## Editing Rules (Anti-Rot Protocol)

To prevent "truth rot," all contributors (human and AI) must follow these rules:

1. **Strict SSOT:** Every fact has exactly one canonical home. **Never re-explain or paraphrase** a concept defined in another doc; use a direct link instead. Duplication-by-paraphrase is a "hallucination trap" and will be rejected.
2. **Reality Only:** Foundation, architecture, and component docs must reflect the current state of the main branch. Never document "planned" or "deferred" features as reality.
3. **Atomic PRs:** A feature and its corresponding documentation changes must land in the same PR.
4. **Silence is Intentional:** If a limitation is not documented, it is a bug in the doc. Explicitly document what a component *cannot* do.

